1
00:00:06,715 --> 00:00:10,886
Life that requires no food
is weak and vulgar!

2
00:00:12,304 --> 00:00:15,099
Life is unpredictable.

3
00:00:15,724 --> 00:00:18,936
You can never eliminate them all.

4
00:00:19,311 --> 00:00:22,773
A small percentage will survive.

5
00:00:45,337 --> 00:00:49,133
<i>You say that they're not the same?</i>

6
00:00:49,216 --> 00:00:51,051
<i>We can't think that.</i>

7
00:00:51,886 --> 00:00:53,179
<i>Never.</i>

8
00:01:02,021 --> 00:01:04,982
What's wrong, Mamoru?

9
00:01:06,025 --> 00:01:07,776
I'm hungry...

10
00:01:08,611 --> 00:01:10,237
You want some?

11
00:01:10,654 --> 00:01:12,490
No, thanks.

12
00:01:14,909 --> 00:01:17,161
They don't taste so good.

13
00:01:18,370 --> 00:01:21,165
But you loved them...

14
00:01:21,665 --> 00:01:24,543
Yeah, I don't know why...

15
00:01:25,377 --> 00:01:27,379
What are you doing?

16
00:01:28,172 --> 00:01:32,510
Nothing... I'm on night watch.

17
00:01:35,054 --> 00:01:39,058
Isn't it cool?
All the team members have one!

18
00:01:43,854 --> 00:01:49,568
You won't quit the team, will you?
We'll always be together.

19
00:01:52,363 --> 00:01:55,908
Well...I don't know.

20
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:02,081
We're different from the rest.

21
00:02:03,749 --> 00:02:05,668
Because we're Amazons?

22
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:08,003
Yes.

23
00:02:09,713 --> 00:02:14,009
But we're not completely
Amazons either.

24
00:02:16,845 --> 00:02:20,182
So where do we belong?

25
00:02:20,349 --> 00:02:22,601
With the team, of course!

26
00:02:27,898 --> 00:02:30,734
I love it here with all the guys!

27
00:02:34,738 --> 00:02:36,448
I don't want this...

28
00:02:38,075 --> 00:02:39,285
What's wrong?

29
00:02:57,011 --> 00:03:01,348
Rain's forecasted for tomorrow
so it will be perfect

30
00:03:01,473 --> 00:03:05,894
but we can't proceed with Tlaloc
while Haruka's around.

31
00:03:07,396 --> 00:03:13,068
<i>Why </i>? Because I don't want
the gas to kill Haruka!

32
00:03:16,196 --> 00:03:22,745
<i>So to protect one Amazon</i>
<i>you'd miss the chance to kill 4,000?</i>

33
00:03:22,911 --> 00:03:26,999
I want him evacuated
so it can go ahead.

34
00:03:28,208 --> 00:03:34,173
If we sedated Haruka with an armlet,
he'd be controllable.

35
00:03:34,632 --> 00:03:36,508
Can you do it?

36
00:03:36,675 --> 00:03:37,968
<i>No.</i>

37
00:03:51,815 --> 00:03:53,025
Damn.

38
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:57,821
Tlaloc is pointless if
it isn't used.

39
00:04:02,368 --> 00:04:04,870
No hot spring resort then?

40
00:04:14,922 --> 00:04:16,757
You could go alone.

41
00:04:28,727 --> 00:04:30,562
How's that?

42
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:42,741
Just this time.

43
00:04:55,379 --> 00:04:56,380
Well?

44
00:04:58,382 --> 00:04:59,216
Oh, sure!

45
00:05:15,983 --> 00:05:17,526
Maybe it's OK.

46
00:06:07,034 --> 00:06:10,829
That prevents us from
hiding here anymore.

47
00:06:11,705 --> 00:06:13,290
We have to run.

48
00:06:13,373 --> 00:06:19,004
But it's scary up there.
It's so dangerous.

49
00:06:28,263 --> 00:06:30,140
Exterminators.

50
00:06:30,307 --> 00:06:32,476
<i>We picked up some signals.</i>

51
00:07:00,963 --> 00:07:01,672
Hello?

52
00:07:01,839 --> 00:07:06,635
<i>Sorry to bother you but</i>
<i>can you come to the office?</i>

53
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:08,470
What is it?

54
00:07:08,595 --> 00:07:10,597
<i>Jin Takayama is here.</i>

55
00:07:10,931 --> 00:07:13,976
He's insisting that
we deploy Tlaloc.

56
00:07:15,435 --> 00:07:16,895
I'm on my way.

57
00:07:28,323 --> 00:07:29,700
Mizuki...

58
00:07:42,921 --> 00:07:46,216
So it's in the underground tunnel.

59
00:07:46,550 --> 00:07:49,636
Rank "A".

60
00:07:50,679 --> 00:07:54,892
We'll surround it.
Haruka goes in from the right.

61
00:07:55,017 --> 00:07:58,228
Kazuya and Mamoru from the left.
Nozomi and I from the side.

62
00:07:59,271 --> 00:08:00,772
Fuku blocks the entrance.

63
00:08:01,398 --> 00:08:02,441
Roger.

64
00:08:03,775 --> 00:08:04,735
Roger.

65
00:08:20,334 --> 00:08:21,585
Kazuya!

66
00:08:27,382 --> 00:08:30,093
Watch out for Mamoru.

67
00:08:30,677 --> 00:08:32,220
Why...?

68
00:08:32,638 --> 00:08:33,972
I don't know.

69
00:08:34,723 --> 00:08:38,518
But remember he's an Amazon too.

70
00:08:40,562 --> 00:08:43,148
Kazuya, come on!

71
00:08:43,273 --> 00:08:45,275
Yeah.

72
00:08:46,443 --> 00:08:50,447
He's different from the test subjects.

73
00:08:51,198 --> 00:08:53,075
Come on, Kazuya!

74
00:08:54,034 --> 00:08:57,788
See? He's the same as usual!

75
00:09:03,335 --> 00:09:04,795
Hurry!

76
00:09:58,807 --> 00:09:59,975
Hey.

77
00:10:01,810 --> 00:10:04,771
- What do you want?
- Tlaloc.

78
00:10:05,355 --> 00:10:08,150
Only you can activate it.

79
00:10:11,194 --> 00:10:13,655
Today's rain will be perfect.

80
00:10:13,739 --> 00:10:16,992
There'll be a better chance.
Please leave.

81
00:10:17,367 --> 00:10:21,705
I don't know what's so special...

82
00:10:21,872 --> 00:10:23,707
about Haruka.

83
00:10:25,751 --> 00:10:29,046
He's the third type of Amazon?

84
00:10:29,755 --> 00:10:34,926
Yes. He's nothing like
other Amazons.

85
00:10:38,555 --> 00:10:40,432
You leave me no choice.

86
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:49,441
I accessed your Amazon database.

87
00:10:49,775 --> 00:10:52,944
With one click I can make it public.

88
00:10:53,070 --> 00:10:56,907
It wasn't hard considering
I used to work here.

89
00:10:59,951 --> 00:11:02,329
Yes, this is blackmail...

90
00:11:05,832 --> 00:11:07,375
Tlaloc.

91
00:11:12,714 --> 00:11:16,426
Let's do it, Director.

92
00:11:32,484 --> 00:11:33,819
A bug.

93
00:11:36,071 --> 00:11:37,656
Another bug.

94
00:11:52,671 --> 00:11:54,047
It's you!

95
00:11:54,339 --> 00:11:55,841
<i>Go on.</i>

96
00:12:00,971 --> 00:12:02,347
You're alive!

97
00:12:03,974 --> 00:12:06,935
All the others died.

98
00:12:08,478 --> 00:12:09,896
You made it...

99
00:12:11,398 --> 00:12:12,649
<i>Haruka.</i>

100
00:12:14,359 --> 00:12:15,819
Is that a bug?

101
00:12:16,444 --> 00:12:18,822
No, it's not!

102
00:12:22,701 --> 00:12:24,995
A bug confirmed.

103
00:12:28,665 --> 00:12:31,209
Haruka, Mamoru.

104
00:12:33,670 --> 00:12:35,046
Run!

105
00:12:36,006 --> 00:12:36,798
But...

106
00:12:37,007 --> 00:12:41,052
Get out that way!
It's not guarded.

107
00:12:49,895 --> 00:12:52,731
<i>It's wrong to kill these people.</i>

108
00:12:54,065 --> 00:12:56,735
<i>Because I am...</i>

109
00:13:01,531 --> 00:13:04,451
Hey, Kazuya.

110
00:13:04,993 --> 00:13:05,952
I'm so hungry.

111
00:13:06,036 --> 00:13:09,080
- But we're hunting!
- Just a little.

112
00:13:09,206 --> 00:13:14,502
You should've eaten up your hamburger.
Hurry up!

113
00:13:16,755 --> 00:13:18,798
Wait up!

114
00:13:39,277 --> 00:13:40,195
Amazon!

115
00:14:07,681 --> 00:14:13,061
You're crazy.
You could get exterminated too.

116
00:14:14,688 --> 00:14:16,314
<i>Ms. Mizusawa.</i>

117
00:14:18,775 --> 00:14:21,236
<i>Activate Tlaloc now.</i>

118
00:14:21,486 --> 00:14:23,196
But Chairman...

119
00:14:24,072 --> 00:14:27,409
<i>Jin Takayama bets his life on it.</i>

120
00:14:27,617 --> 00:14:31,496
<i>You should stand by your project.</i>

121
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:35,834
<i>An unrealized accomplishment</i>
<i>is worthless!</i>

122
00:14:37,794 --> 00:14:40,171
<i>I want to see it!</i>

123
00:14:40,755 --> 00:14:45,510
<i>I want to see what will happen</i>
<i>with a test of this scale.</i>

124
00:14:50,515 --> 00:14:53,101
A test of this scale!

125
00:14:53,852 --> 00:14:56,688
You're the craziest one.

126
00:14:58,315 --> 00:15:00,317
<i>Ms. Mizusawa.</i>

127
00:15:20,545 --> 00:15:24,883
Very well. Kano, get ready.

128
00:15:39,689 --> 00:15:42,150
<i>Where is Haruka?</i>

129
00:15:59,417 --> 00:16:00,752
Haruka?

130
00:16:12,597 --> 00:16:14,099
Haruka!

131
00:16:17,102 --> 00:16:18,353
What now?

132
00:16:18,728 --> 00:16:22,232
We'll go somewhere...

133
00:16:28,363 --> 00:16:31,241
I'm sorry. You have to go!

134
00:16:31,950 --> 00:16:35,703
I can't stop myself!

135
00:16:45,380 --> 00:16:46,798
Sorry...

136
00:16:48,133 --> 00:16:49,217
Let's go.

137
00:17:30,258 --> 00:17:32,552
<i>Research here. There are signals.</i>

138
00:17:33,303 --> 00:17:35,597
<i>They're all around you.</i>

139
00:17:35,722 --> 00:17:39,517
<i>The same type are awakening.</i>
<i>They're Rank "E".</i>

140
00:17:40,226 --> 00:17:42,729
<i>We read 246 signals.</i>

141
00:17:42,854 --> 00:17:44,272
Shit!

142
00:17:45,690 --> 00:17:46,608
Shido here!

143
00:17:46,983 --> 00:17:52,697
This is Mizusawa.
I just deployed Tlaloc.

144
00:17:55,825 --> 00:17:56,784
No warning?

145
00:17:56,868 --> 00:17:58,995
<i>It's a long story.</i>

146
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:01,456
Evacuate Haruka and "M".

147
00:18:06,878 --> 00:18:11,716
Haruka, Mamoru!
Leave the bugs and pull out!

148
00:18:12,592 --> 00:18:14,761
Haruka! Mamoru!

149
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:26,272
Haruka!

150
00:18:26,814 --> 00:18:28,691
Nozomi, stop him!

151
00:18:28,816 --> 00:18:31,861
Kazuya, get Mamoru out of the city!

152
00:18:31,986 --> 00:18:35,782
Roger! Mamoru, we're out of here!

153
00:18:37,075 --> 00:18:39,619
Mamoru, come on!

154
00:18:49,295 --> 00:18:50,505
Kazuya.

155
00:18:53,091 --> 00:18:54,175
Kazuya.

156
00:18:56,386 --> 00:18:57,136
Kazuya!

157
00:18:57,428 --> 00:18:58,763
Yes?

158
00:19:40,346 --> 00:19:43,308
I put so much into creating
you guys...

159
00:19:45,059 --> 00:19:46,936
That's why...

160
00:19:49,939 --> 00:19:54,027
You're like my babies.
I mean it.

161
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:58,781
But...

162
00:20:00,408 --> 00:20:06,414
None of us expected to be eaten
by our creations.

163
00:20:07,749 --> 00:20:10,001
There's no place for you to be.

164
00:20:12,128 --> 00:20:13,630
Sorry.

165
00:20:17,175 --> 00:20:18,801
No place on earth

166
00:20:20,762 --> 00:20:23,848
but I'll make sure
you go to hell.

167
00:20:30,855 --> 00:20:32,482
<i>Alpha.</i>

168
00:20:48,164 --> 00:20:49,207
Amazon.

169
00:21:28,579 --> 00:21:29,831
Haruka!

170
00:21:31,666 --> 00:21:32,917
Why are you here?

171
00:21:33,668 --> 00:21:35,086
I brought you this!

172
00:21:39,215 --> 00:21:44,220
I'm so hungry.
Let me eat that girl.

173
00:21:49,559 --> 00:21:50,935
Help me...

174
00:21:51,269 --> 00:21:52,979
I want to eat her!

175
00:21:54,230 --> 00:21:57,775
I'm sorry but I can't help
you anymore.

176
00:21:57,942 --> 00:22:00,278
You can't have Mizuki.

177
00:22:01,571 --> 00:22:02,447
Haruka!

178
00:22:02,613 --> 00:22:05,867
I know it sounds cold
but that's who I am.

179
00:22:06,033 --> 00:22:08,870
I'll listen to my internal voice!

180
00:22:37,815 --> 00:22:39,108
Get out!

181
00:22:39,275 --> 00:22:40,610
Tlaloc has begun!

182
00:22:45,740 --> 00:22:47,909
Haruka!

183
00:23:25,947 --> 00:23:28,241
Kazuya!

184
00:23:28,616 --> 00:23:29,826
Kazuya?

185
00:23:32,453 --> 00:23:35,456
What's wrong?

186
00:24:23,546 --> 00:24:24,672
Kazuya!

187
00:24:30,344 --> 00:24:34,724
Just a little bit, Kazuya.

188
00:24:46,944 --> 00:24:48,237
Mamoru!

189
00:24:49,280 --> 00:24:51,782
Mamoru, don't eat it!

190
00:24:53,284 --> 00:24:54,368
Mamoru!

191
00:25:20,895 --> 00:25:23,606
His armlet's blue!

192
00:25:30,947 --> 00:25:32,239
Mamoru.

193
00:25:42,291 --> 00:25:43,626
Mamoru.

194
00:25:48,589 --> 00:25:50,257
Kazuya...?

195
00:25:54,261 --> 00:25:55,471
Mamoru...

196
00:26:18,661 --> 00:26:19,870
What have I...

197
00:26:30,798 --> 00:26:31,757
Mamoru!

198
00:26:37,471 --> 00:26:39,640
Kazuya!

199
00:26:40,891 --> 00:26:41,892
Shido!

200
00:26:44,186 --> 00:26:46,313
That's bullshit!

201
00:26:46,814 --> 00:26:48,607
Where is Mamoru?

202
00:26:50,901 --> 00:26:52,319
Headed for exit #3.

203
00:26:54,238 --> 00:26:55,698
Mamoru!

204
00:27:00,411 --> 00:27:01,537
Run!

205
00:27:06,459 --> 00:27:08,461
Run, Haruka!

206
00:27:29,148 --> 00:27:30,524
Haruka...

207
00:27:37,364 --> 00:27:40,326
Please go with this thing!

208
00:27:54,048 --> 00:27:55,508
Mizuki.

209
00:27:56,801 --> 00:28:02,139
Thanks. You know I'm an Amazon but
you treat me the same.

210
00:28:17,196 --> 00:28:19,323
I'll find Mamoru.

211
00:28:21,951 --> 00:28:27,081
Haruka, wait! Don't go!

212
00:28:27,706 --> 00:28:29,125
Don't!

213
00:29:03,325 --> 00:29:04,827
Come on!

214
00:30:10,851 --> 00:30:12,269
Amazon!
